780734e","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_big_o_and_little_o_notations_c490e3b9_009","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which of the following big-O or little-o claims, with the limiting directions shown, is false?","options":["$\\sin x=o(x)$ as $x\\to+\\infty$","$2^x=O(x^2)$ as $x\\to+\\infty$","$x^2=o(x)$ as $x\\to0$","$x=O(\\sin x)$ as $x\\to0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9241d579b3093cd1270f7469","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_big_o_and_little_o_notations_c490e3b9_012","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $f(x)=o(x^2)$ and $g(x)=o(x^3)$ as $x\\to0$. Which statement about $(f(x)+g(x))^2$ is guaranteed?","options":["It is $O(x^6)$ as $x\\to0$.","It is $o(x^4)$ as $x\\to0$.","It is $o(x^5)$ as $x\\to0$.","It is $o(x^6)$ as $x\\to0$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9094f5c35229e9421164cbab","time_limit":30},{"id":"expansion_big_o_and_little_o_notations_014","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What limit defines $f(x)=o(g(x))$ as $x\\to a$?","options":["$\\lim_{x\\to a}f(x)/g(x)=1$","$\\lim_{x\\to a}g(x)/f(x)=0$","$\\lim_{x\\to a}f(x)/g(x)=0$","$\\lim_{x\\to a}f(x)=\\infty$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"086bf498b630e1a934f74a43","time_limit":20},{"id":"expansion_big_o_and_little_o_notations_020","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"As $x\\to0$, what is true for $f(x)=5x^4$ and $g(x)=x^2$?","options":["$f(x)=o(g(x))$","$g(x)=o(f(x))$","$f(x)/g(x)\\to5$","$f(x)$ is not $O(g(x))$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9ff66e5aba659ded158dcdd9","time_limit":30},{"id":"expansion_big_o_and_little_o_notations_013_curated20261027_001","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $f,g\\colon\\mathbb{R}\\to\\mathbb{R}$ and $a\\in\\mathbb{R}$. Which statement is the definition of $f(x)=O(g(x))$ as $x\\to a$?","options":["Some $M>0$ satisfies $|f(x)|\\le M\\,|g(x)|$ for all $x$ in a punctured neighbourhood of $a$.","Some $M>0$ satisfies $|f(x)|\\le M\\,|g(x)|$ for all $x\\in\\mathbb{R}$, not only near $a$.","$|f(x)|\\le|g(x)|$ holds for all $x$ in a punctured neighbourhood of $a$, with no constant allowed.","$\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to a}\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)}=1$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"dab10747b36e6d61ed4c238c","time_limit":40},{"id":"expansion_big_o_and_little_o_notations_015_curated20261027_002","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $a\\in\\mathbb{R}$ and $g(x)\\neq0$ near $a$. Which statement implies $f(x)=O(g(x))$ as $x\\to a$, but is not implied by it?","options":["$g(x)=O(f(x))$ as $x\\to a$","$|f(x)|\\ge c\\,|g(x)|$ near $a$ for some $c>0$","$f(x)=o(g(x))$ as $x\\to a$","$f(a)=g(a)$ at the point $a$ itself"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"fad73512eb3a475454a7d9d1","time_limit":35},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_big_o_and_little_o_notations_c490e3b9_topup20261028_001","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $f,h\\colon\\mathbb{R}\\to\\mathbb{R}$ satisfy $f(x)=O(x)$ and $h(x)=O(x)$ as $x\\to0$. Which conclusion holds for every such pair $f,h$?","options":["$f(x)+h(x)=O(x)$ as $x\\to0$","$f(x)=h(x)$ for all $x$ near $0$","$f(x)=O(h(x))$ as $x\\to0$","$f(x)-h(x)=o(x)$ as $x\\to0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"8e37572fdb5b6f47a0c64f29","time_limit":35},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_big_o_and_little_o_notations_c490e3b9_topup20261028_002","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Define $f(x)=x\\sin(1/x)$ for $x\\neq0$ and $f(0)=0$. Which statement about $f$ compared with $x$ as $x\\to0$ is correct?","options":["$f(x)=o(x)$, because $f(x)\\to0$ as $x\\to0$.","$f(x)$ is not $O(x)$, because $f(x)/x$ has no limit as $x\\to0$.","$f(x)\\sim x$, because $|f(x)|\\le|x|$ for all $x\\neq0$.","$f(x)=O(x)$, although $f(x)/x$ has no limit as $x\\to0$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"cd763adc616b4b79184e8a61","time_limit":45},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_big_o_and_little_o_notations_c490e3b9_topup20261028_003","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"As $x\\to0$, let $f(x)=3x+r_1(x)$ and $g(x)=2x+r_2(x)$, where $r_1(x)=o(x)$ and $r_2(x)=o(x)$. What can be said about $\\lim_{x\\to0}f(x)/g(x)$?","options":["It equals $1$, since $f$ and $g$ are both of order $x$.","It equals $\\frac{3}{2}$, whatever the functions $r_1,r_2$ are.","It does not exist, since $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ both tend to $0$.","It depends on which functions $r_1$ and $r_2$ are."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"f2019774537c5b41ed0c490a","time_limit":45}]}}